<mxCell id="e32" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n15" target="n16"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="n33" value="FINDING C1 (High). JWT_SECRET_KEY is empty in .env and .env.example, with no default and no startup guard. issue_access_token() then raises &#x27;HMAC key must not be empty&#x27; → 500 on the FIRST successful OTP. This also makes all 5 test_mobed_api tests fail under the documented &#x27;uv run pytest&#x27;." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="1140" width="320" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e34" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#b85450;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.2;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n15" target="n33"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="140" value="FINDING C2 (Med). The seeded demo agyary has no wa_phone_number_id, so onboarding to it 400s here. Combined with C1 and empty Flow ids, the documented dev/demo path for the PWA cannot actually be walked by hand." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="260" width="320" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e35" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#b85450;exitX=1;exitY=0.2;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.2;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n6" target="140"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="n36" value="FINDING D1 (Med). Doc 05: &#x27;joining additional agyaries is a standing action from their own menu.&#x27; The API (/agyaries/{id}/join) exists, but the PWA never calls it — there is no join-another-agyari screen. A multi-agyari mobed can only ever belong to the one they onboarded with." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;size=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1060" y="1330" width="320" height="150" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="e37" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;dashed=1;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#d6b656;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.2;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n16" target="n36"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
